          %p
            Pre-abelian and abelian categories are sometimes called (AB1) and (AB2) categories, after the sequence of additional axioms on top of additive categories introduced by Grothendieck in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tohoku"} Tohoku
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Coim
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi f
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Im
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Coim}\,f\to \mathrm{Im}\,f
            is an isomorphism). These continue in non-selfdual manner:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                AB3: an abelian category with all coproducts (hence with all
                = succeed "s);" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %li
              %p AB4: an (AB3) category in which coproducts of monomorphisms are monic;
            %li
              %p
                AB5: an (AB3) category in which
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
                of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
            %li
              %p AB6: an (AB3) category such that
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    For any object
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    in the category and any family
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi j
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi j
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B^j)_{j\in J}
                    of increasing directed families of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msubsup
                            %mi B
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %msub
                                %mi I
                                %mi j
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^i=(B_i^j)_{i\in I_j}
                    of
                    = succeed "s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi j
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^j
                    of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                              %mrow
                                %mi j
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi J
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msub
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %msub
                                    %mi I
                                    %mi j
                              %msubsup
                                %mi B
                                %mi j
                                %mi i
                              %mo )
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∈
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                                %msub
                                  %mi I
                                  %mi j
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msub
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                                %mrow
                                  %mi j
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi J
                              %msubsup
                                %mi B
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi j
                                %mi i
                              %mo )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap_{j\in J}\left(\sum_{i\in I_j}B_j^i\right)=\sum_{(i_j)\in \prod I_j}\left(\bigcap_{j\in J}B_{i_j}^i\right)
                %li
                  %p Notice that this implies that inf for any family of subobjects exists.
          %p
            We have a chain of implications AB6
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇒
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
            AB5
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇒
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
            AB4, see (
            %a{:href => "#Popescu73"}> Nicolae Popescu 1973, Sect. 2.8, Corollaries 8.9, 8.13
            ).
          %p The concepts (AB3–AB6) also have dual forms (AB3*–AB6*).
          %p There are further refinements along these lines. In particular
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+category"}> Grothendieck category
              \: an (AB5) category with a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generator"} generator
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#Popescu73"}> Nicolae Popescu 1973, Sect. 2.8, Theorem 8.6
                )
              %br/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be an AB3-category. The following assertions are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  is AB5.
              %li
                %p
                  For any direct set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo }
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\{X_i\right\}_i
                  of subobjects of any object
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo :
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j: \underset{\rightarrow}{\lim} X_i \rightarrow X
                  defined such that
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %msub
                            %mi u
                            %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi j
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j u_i=j_i
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi u
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_i: X_i \rightarrow \underset{\rightarrow}{\lim} X_i
                  are structural morphisms and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi j
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_i: X_i \rightarrow X
                  are canonical inclusions) is an isomorphism of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\rightarrow}{\lim} X_i
                  onto
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_i X_i
              %li
                %p
                  Let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  be any object,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo }
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\{X_i\right\}_i
                  a direct set of subobjects, and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                            %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{\prime}
                  a subobject of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                          %mo ∩
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                              %mo ′
                          %mo )
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                        %mo ∩
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                            %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\sum_i\left(X_i \cap X^{\prime}\right)=\left(\sum_i X_i\right) \cap X^{\prime}
              %li
                %p
                  Let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: Y \rightarrow X
                  be a morphism and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo }
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\{X_i\right\}_i
                  a direct set of subobjects of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                        %mo =
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f^{-1}\left(\sum_i X_i\right)=\sum_i f^{-1}\left(X_i\right)
              %li
                %p
                  Let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\{X_i\right\}_{i \in I}
                  be a set of objects. For any finite subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_F
                  image of canonical morphism
                  = succeed "," do
